WEBVTT

00:00:01.835 --> 00:00:03.879
Futurama is brought to you by...

00:00:04.588 --> 00:00:06.215
Glagnar's Human Rinds.

00:00:06.298 --> 00:00:08.550
It's a buncha muncha cruncha humans!

00:01:00.864 --> 00:01:03.075
Aw! Somebody likes snouts.

00:01:03.274 --> 00:01:04.275
Is it me?

00:01:08.176 --> 00:01:10.679
Oh, my head! My precious head!

00:01:11.096 --> 00:01:12.097
Oh!

00:01:13.931 --> 00:01:16.183
Stupid can opener!

00:01:16.268 --> 00:01:19.146
You killed my father
and now you've come back for me!

00:01:19.229 --> 00:01:20.397
You all right, Bender?

00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:22.232
Yeah, I guess so.

00:01:22.315 --> 00:01:25.444
But I don't see why we keep
this ticking time bomb around

00:01:25.527 --> 00:01:27.154
just for that dumb animal!

00:01:27.237 --> 00:01:29.072
Don't yell at Nibbler like that.

00:01:29.156 --> 00:01:30.449
You hurt his feelings.

00:01:30.532 --> 00:01:32.576
Come on, pet him and make up.

00:01:32.659 --> 00:01:35.329
- No.
- I said pet him.

00:01:35.896 --> 00:01:37.522
I'll pet him.

00:01:37.606 --> 00:01:39.691
I'll pet him with both hands!

00:01:40.067 --> 00:01:42.027
Ow, my ass!

00:01:42.110 --> 00:01:43.487
Get off! get off!

00:01:43.570 --> 00:01:44.655
Are you all right?

00:01:44.738 --> 00:01:47.032
It's nothing a lawsuit won't cure.

00:01:47.115 --> 00:01:48.408
Not you.

00:01:50.577 --> 00:01:52.621
Aw! Poor baby.

00:01:52.704 --> 00:01:54.081
Chipped a fang.

00:01:55.707 --> 00:01:57.459
Hey, I got a busted ass here!

00:01:57.584 --> 00:01:59.336
I don't see anyone kissing it!

00:01:59.419 --> 00:02:02.130
All right, I'm coming.

00:02:14.151 --> 00:02:15.569
Remember, Rover gets the pill,

00:02:15.652 --> 00:02:17.696
and Pepper gets the suppository.

00:02:17.779 --> 00:02:18.989
Next!

00:02:23.201 --> 00:02:24.286
Ow!

00:02:26.038 --> 00:02:28.248
It's just a simple broken fang.
Nothing serious.

00:02:28.332 --> 00:02:30.042
What's that you say there, Doctor?

00:02:30.125 --> 00:02:31.918
You're going to have to put him down?

00:02:32.002 --> 00:02:33.712
No, I... But I...

00:02:33.795 --> 00:02:35.255
Terrible shame, that.

00:02:35.339 --> 00:02:36.798
Shall I do the honors?

00:02:38.800 --> 00:02:39.801
No!

00:02:41.845 --> 00:02:43.013
You about done?

00:02:43.096 --> 00:02:45.015
Next time I'm keeping it.

00:02:45.474 --> 00:02:47.517
I believe I have
a replacement fang for your pet

00:02:47.601 --> 00:02:48.936
in the next room.

00:02:58.487 --> 00:02:59.696
Oh!

00:02:59.780 --> 00:03:01.281
The jaguar didn't want to cooperate,

00:03:01.365 --> 00:03:03.992
but luckily he knocked
one of my teeth out.

00:03:04.076 --> 00:03:05.410
Now, then...

00:03:05.744 --> 00:03:06.787
Ow!

00:03:08.872 --> 00:03:11.541
Hey, what are these rings
in Nibbler's fang?

00:03:11.875 --> 00:03:15.212
Um... I'm still a little woozy
from a gazelle kick this morning,

00:03:15.295 --> 00:03:19.216
but if he's anything like the common tree
the rings might indicate his age.

00:03:19.299 --> 00:03:21.176
Yeah, well, good luck.

00:03:21.259 --> 00:03:24.179
It would take some kind of genius
to count all those rings.

00:03:24.262 --> 00:03:25.847
He's five.

00:03:28.642 --> 00:03:31.019
Happy birthday, young Nibbler.

00:03:32.479 --> 00:03:35.691
Aw! Look how cuddly
he looks in his new cape.

00:03:35.774 --> 00:03:38.652
I'd be cuddly, too,
if someone gave me a new cape.

00:03:38.735 --> 00:03:41.822
Who's playing "pin the tail
on the moon maggot"?

00:03:41.905 --> 00:03:44.283
Ooh! Me! Everyone watch how good I am!

00:03:59.298 --> 00:04:02.384
Yay! And the crowd goes wild!

00:04:02.467 --> 00:04:04.261
What prize do I get? Cash?

00:04:04.344 --> 00:04:06.013
Hey, look at Nibbler.

00:04:08.473 --> 00:04:10.225
Aw! He's holding a spoon.

00:04:10.309 --> 00:04:12.352
He's so talented.

00:04:12.436 --> 00:04:13.812
You call that talent?

00:04:13.895 --> 00:04:15.230
Gather 'round ol' Bender

00:04:15.314 --> 00:04:17.816
and get ready for the show of a lifetime.

00:04:28.243 --> 00:04:29.745
Ta-da!

00:04:31.079 --> 00:04:34.124
Now, he's wearing a hat!

00:04:34.207 --> 00:04:36.627
Come on, let's all sing "Happy Birthday."

00:04:36.710 --> 00:04:39.296
What day is today

00:04:39.379 --> 00:04:41.923
It's Nibbler's birthday

00:04:42.007 --> 00:04:44.718
What a day for a birthday

00:04:44.801 --> 00:04:47.596
Let's all have some cake

00:04:47.679 --> 00:04:50.474
And you smell like one, too

00:04:53.352 --> 00:04:54.853
Hey! What about this?

00:04:56.697 --> 00:05:00.033
Bender, I thought you were
supposed to be cooking for this party.

00:05:00.117 --> 00:05:02.619
Fine. We'll have rack of Nibbler.

00:05:02.703 --> 00:05:04.287
Just make a simple cake.

00:05:04.371 --> 00:05:06.957
And this time
if someone's going to jump out of it,

00:05:07.040 --> 00:05:09.668
make sure to put them in
after you cook it.

00:05:09.751 --> 00:05:11.962
So it's a cake you want, is it?

00:05:12.462 --> 00:05:16.341
I'll make you a cake you'll never forget.

00:05:21.430 --> 00:05:23.682
That'll take care of those annoying rats.

00:05:23.765 --> 00:05:26.143
Now, to make a cake so delicious

00:05:26.226 --> 00:05:29.354
they'll have no choice
but to love and worship me.

00:05:59.301 --> 00:06:03.180
There. This will teach
those filthy bastards who's lovable.

00:06:03.680 --> 00:06:05.640
Now, all I have to do is spell check it,

00:06:05.724 --> 00:06:08.435
and it's ready for my admiring public.

00:06:14.775 --> 00:06:16.652
No! Get away from there.

00:06:24.076 --> 00:06:26.286
That's it.

00:06:28.246 --> 00:06:30.248
Happy birthday.

00:06:35.295 --> 00:06:37.255
Bender, what's going...

00:06:38.674 --> 00:06:40.300
No!

00:06:40.384 --> 00:06:42.719
Hey, can't you see I'm using the toilet?

00:06:49.893 --> 00:06:53.438
Bender, how could you
flush Nibbler down the toilet?

00:06:53.522 --> 00:06:55.440
Well, step one, I had to lift the seat.

00:06:55.524 --> 00:06:57.484
That was the first little annoyance.

00:06:57.567 --> 00:06:58.902
Am I right, men?

00:06:59.820 --> 00:07:01.363
Aren't you upset at all?

00:07:01.446 --> 00:07:04.449
How would you feel if I
flushed Fry down the toilet?

00:07:04.533 --> 00:07:06.201
Only one way to find out.

00:07:07.411 --> 00:07:10.372
You have no sympathy
for anyone else's feelings.

00:07:10.455 --> 00:07:11.540
Of course I do.

00:07:11.623 --> 00:07:13.667
Right now, I feel sorry for you.

00:07:13.750 --> 00:07:15.419
- You do?
- Yeah. I mean,

00:07:15.502 --> 00:07:18.130
one cantaloupe-sized bloodshot eye.

00:07:18.213 --> 00:07:21.091
You ain't winning
no beauty pageants, lady.

00:07:25.095 --> 00:07:29.141
And so we say good-bye
to our beloved pet Nibbler,

00:07:29.224 --> 00:07:33.729
who's gone to a place where I, too,
hope one day to go.

00:07:33.812 --> 00:07:34.980
The toilet.

00:07:46.032 --> 00:07:47.450
I wouldn't feel so bad

00:07:47.807 --> 00:07:51.352
if Bender just understood
the pain he caused me.

00:07:53.874 --> 00:07:55.584
Give it to me straight, doctor.

00:07:55.667 --> 00:07:57.210
Don't sugarcoat it.

00:07:57.294 --> 00:07:58.754
Very well.

00:07:58.837 --> 00:08:00.088
Your entire family died

00:08:00.213 --> 00:08:04.301
when a plane piloted by your fiancée
crashed into your uninsured home.

00:08:04.384 --> 00:08:06.178
And you have inoperable cancer.

00:08:08.972 --> 00:08:11.391
Bet you weren't expecting
that one, Calculon!

00:08:11.475 --> 00:08:14.561
It's like he doesn't understand
simple humanoid emotion.

00:08:14.644 --> 00:08:18.315
I wish just once Bender could feel
exactly what I feel.

00:08:18.398 --> 00:08:20.734
Actually, through the miracle of science,

00:08:20.817 --> 00:08:22.152
that can be arranged.

00:08:22.235 --> 00:08:24.946
Uh-oh. Is this gonna be
another crazy experiment

00:08:25.030 --> 00:08:27.366
that crosses a line
man was not meant to cross?

00:08:29.117 --> 00:08:30.619
The official death toll

00:08:30.702 --> 00:08:34.665
in that tragic rocket crash
has now been raised to 54,000.

00:08:37.651 --> 00:08:40.779
Hey, what the hell
are you doing with my head?

00:08:40.862 --> 00:08:42.322
I need to tinker in it.

00:08:42.406 --> 00:08:44.992
Why don't you just use
a potted plant like Fry?

00:08:45.075 --> 00:08:46.285
Quiet you.

00:08:46.368 --> 00:08:48.287
I'm installing an empathy chip.

00:08:48.370 --> 00:08:51.039
And that'll allow Bender
to feel other people's emotions?

00:08:51.123 --> 00:08:54.251
Yes. If by "allow" you mean "force."

00:08:55.252 --> 00:08:56.962
- Son of a... Careful with that!
- Oh, dear.

00:08:57.087 --> 00:08:59.298
- Oh, my.
- Hey!

00:08:59.381 --> 00:09:01.091
Once more. My bad.

00:09:01.174 --> 00:09:02.593
Steady now.

00:09:02.676 --> 00:09:03.844
There we go.

00:09:06.013 --> 00:09:10.183
Now, I'll simply tune it
to Leela's emotional frequency.

00:09:11.727 --> 00:09:12.895
My God.

00:09:12.978 --> 00:09:15.814
I'm overcome with feelings.

00:09:15.939 --> 00:09:18.901
I'm experiencing a powerful yearning to...

00:09:18.984 --> 00:09:22.112
To cram my gullet full of mackerel heads.

00:09:22.195 --> 00:09:23.614
That's me, baby.

00:09:23.739 --> 00:09:25.073
Hmm.

00:09:25.699 --> 00:09:28.243
Now I'm worried that
I'm not as smart as Leela.

00:09:28.327 --> 00:09:29.828
But at the same time,

00:09:29.912 --> 00:09:32.122
I feel relieved that I'm cuter than her.

00:09:32.247 --> 00:09:33.957
Uh... That's me.

00:09:34.041 --> 00:09:35.125
Thanks for covering.

00:09:36.251 --> 00:09:38.003
This time I miss Nibbler,

00:09:38.086 --> 00:09:40.297
and I'm feeling nosy and opinionated.

00:09:40.380 --> 00:09:41.715
- Bingo.
- That's Leela.

00:09:41.798 --> 00:09:42.966
Thank you, Professor.

00:09:43.050 --> 00:09:45.719
I'm happy that Bender
can finally feel my pain.

00:09:45.802 --> 00:09:48.055
Happy. I like this feeling.

00:09:48.138 --> 00:09:50.891
Just don't revert
to your usual mopey self.

00:09:50.974 --> 00:09:53.268
I'm not mopey. You shut up.

00:09:53.352 --> 00:09:54.478
Anger, huh?

00:09:54.561 --> 00:09:56.521
How dare you make me feel anger,

00:09:56.605 --> 00:09:58.857
you one-eyed jerk with a dead pet!

00:10:08.992 --> 00:10:11.036
Thanks for taking me out, Amy.

00:10:11.119 --> 00:10:13.080
I feel slightly less miserable already.

00:10:13.163 --> 00:10:15.207
Hey, you know what would cheer you up?

00:10:15.290 --> 00:10:17.000
You should get yourself a puppy.

00:10:17.084 --> 00:10:18.126
A puppy?

00:10:19.127 --> 00:10:21.588
Nibbler loved to eat puppies.

00:10:24.549 --> 00:10:25.968
What's your problem?

00:10:26.426 --> 00:10:29.096
- I miss Nibbler.
- You do?

00:10:29.179 --> 00:10:30.222
Hell, no!

00:10:30.305 --> 00:10:31.682
It's Leela's stupid feelings.

00:10:31.765 --> 00:10:33.684
Why can't she just drink herself happy

00:10:33.767 --> 00:10:35.352
like a normal person?

00:10:44.945 --> 00:10:46.280
Uh-oh, jealousy.

00:10:46.572 --> 00:10:48.407
You think you're so hot!

00:10:48.657 --> 00:10:50.784
- Huh?
- The only reason you get all the guys

00:10:50.867 --> 00:10:52.911
is because you dress like a tramp.

00:10:53.870 --> 00:10:56.582
They're just responding to my personality.

00:10:57.374 --> 00:10:59.543
Um, Leela, Armando and I

00:10:59.626 --> 00:11:02.212
are going to the backseat
of his car for coffee.

00:11:02.296 --> 00:11:04.590
You going to be all right
here by yourself?

00:11:04.673 --> 00:11:06.925
Sure. I'm having a great time.

00:11:07.009 --> 00:11:09.595
Really, you two go enjoy yourselves.

00:11:11.471 --> 00:11:13.140
I'm so lonely.

00:11:13.223 --> 00:11:15.893
I'm going to go eat a bucket of ice cream.

00:11:19.730 --> 00:11:21.732
The spoon's in the foot powder.

00:11:30.574 --> 00:11:32.326
I'm at the end of my rope.

00:11:32.409 --> 00:11:36.413
I can't live another minute
without poor, sweet Nibbler.

00:11:36.496 --> 00:11:37.873
Too bad he wasn't an alligator.

00:11:37.956 --> 00:11:40.667
When you flush those things
they stay alive in the sewers.

00:11:40.751 --> 00:11:42.127
- Really?
- Yep.

00:11:42.210 --> 00:11:44.630
My friend's cousin's
caseworker saw one once.

00:11:44.713 --> 00:11:46.089
It's a widely believed fact.

00:11:46.381 --> 00:11:47.591
Hmm.

00:11:47.674 --> 00:11:49.051
Sewers.

00:11:49.134 --> 00:11:51.178
Thinking, thinking, thinking.

00:11:52.471 --> 00:11:55.474
Hang on, Nibbler!
Uncle Bender's coming to save you.

00:11:59.353 --> 00:12:00.979
Damn, it's too small.

00:12:01.063 --> 00:12:03.690
What do those humans
design this for, anyway?

00:12:08.070 --> 00:12:09.279
Aha!

00:12:09.363 --> 00:12:11.823
Bender, one. Toilet, zero.

00:12:15.118 --> 00:12:17.329
See you on the other side.

00:12:19.873 --> 00:12:21.500
Bender? Bender?

00:12:22.542 --> 00:12:23.919
Have you seen my sombrero?

00:12:29.716 --> 00:12:32.010
Now he's flushed himself down the toilet?

00:12:32.094 --> 00:12:33.387
Who's he going to flush next?

00:12:33.470 --> 00:12:34.846
Hey, it's your fault.

00:12:34.930 --> 00:12:35.931
He only flushed himself

00:12:36.014 --> 00:12:37.808
because your emotions made him feel bad.

00:12:37.891 --> 00:12:38.934
You're right.

00:12:39.017 --> 00:12:40.227
I feel terrible.

00:12:40.310 --> 00:12:41.311
Oh, great.

00:12:41.395 --> 00:12:42.980
Now you're making him feel worse.

00:12:43.063 --> 00:12:45.816
I guess we'd better go down
into the sewers and look for him.

00:12:45.899 --> 00:12:47.234
Are you crazy?

00:12:47.317 --> 00:12:48.777
There's mutants down there.

00:12:48.860 --> 00:12:49.945
They'll eat you alive.

00:12:50.028 --> 00:12:51.655
They're hideous!

00:12:54.241 --> 00:12:56.201
There's no such thing as mutants.

00:12:56.285 --> 00:12:58.078
That's a ridiculous urban myth.

00:12:58.161 --> 00:13:00.289
Oh, don't be so sure.

00:13:00.372 --> 00:13:04.126
Many scientists believe
humans really could mutate down there

00:13:04.209 --> 00:13:09.047
due to exposure to toxic waste
and radioactive runoff

00:13:09.131 --> 00:13:11.550
and good old American feces.

00:13:11.633 --> 00:13:13.802
God bless America.

00:13:21.518 --> 00:13:22.895
Ladies first.

00:13:27.232 --> 00:13:29.276
Ugh! And the aftertaste.

00:13:34.239 --> 00:13:36.033
- What is it?
- I burned my finger.

00:13:37.284 --> 00:13:38.911
Okay, check the guidebook.

00:13:38.994 --> 00:13:40.704
Looks like we're under Park Avenue.

00:13:41.413 --> 00:13:43.165
Ooh! Ritzy.

00:13:43.248 --> 00:13:47.294
Just think, all this was probably once
s charity luncheon for the Met.

00:13:48.503 --> 00:13:49.504
Wait, what's that?

00:13:51.465 --> 00:13:53.717
I never should have thrown out the manual.

00:13:53.800 --> 00:13:56.803
Bender, you didn't have to come down here.

00:13:56.887 --> 00:14:00.515
I know, but I just missed Nibbler so much.

00:14:02.476 --> 00:14:04.019
He was so cute.

00:14:04.102 --> 00:14:05.687
He was so sweet.

00:14:06.772 --> 00:14:09.441
This emotional display
is making me nauseous.

00:14:10.108 --> 00:14:11.735
Or maybe it's whatever that is.

00:14:12.986 --> 00:14:14.780
Nibbler!

00:14:14.863 --> 00:14:16.949
Nibbler!

00:14:17.115 --> 00:14:20.327
It's no use. We better turn back.

00:14:20.410 --> 00:14:21.787
Which way, Fry?

00:14:22.037 --> 00:14:25.249
Hmm. According to this map,
the only way out is through...

00:14:25.332 --> 00:14:26.333
That pipe.

00:14:29.253 --> 00:14:31.505
Don't worry, it gets wider
after about a mile.

00:14:31.588 --> 00:14:33.131
- Idiot.
- Idiot.

00:14:33.507 --> 00:14:35.509
Okay, okay, never mind.

00:14:35.592 --> 00:14:37.386
I'll just ask those people for directions.

00:14:40.472 --> 00:14:41.598
Mutants!

00:14:50.148 --> 00:14:52.109
Mutants! They're real.

00:14:53.986 --> 00:14:55.612
I'll take care of this.

00:14:56.655 --> 00:14:58.115
Back. Back.

00:15:01.076 --> 00:15:02.452
Thanks, handsome.

00:15:02.536 --> 00:15:04.955
Please, do not be frightened.
We're harmless.

00:15:05.038 --> 00:15:06.331
I have three arms.

00:15:06.415 --> 00:15:07.916
I said harmless, not armless.

00:15:08.000 --> 00:15:10.669
Lay off him.
You know he's only got one ear.

00:15:10.752 --> 00:15:12.754
Hey, aren't you supposed
to be eating our brains?

00:15:12.838 --> 00:15:13.839
You're mutants.

00:15:13.922 --> 00:15:14.965
Mutants?

00:15:15.048 --> 00:15:17.342
Perhaps it is you who are the mutants.

00:15:17.426 --> 00:15:18.886
Please, Dwayne.

00:15:18.969 --> 00:15:20.971
Have you looked in a mirror lately?

00:15:22.472 --> 00:15:24.057
Welcome to our village.

00:15:24.141 --> 00:15:27.728
It may not be Paris,
but it has a certain quaint charm

00:15:27.811 --> 00:15:29.813
that I, for one,
wouldn't trade for the world.

00:15:29.897 --> 00:15:32.149
You guys realize
you live in a sewer, right?

00:15:32.232 --> 00:15:33.233
Perhaps.

00:15:33.317 --> 00:15:34.985
But perhaps your civilization

00:15:35.068 --> 00:15:38.530
is merely the sewer
of an even greater society above you.

00:15:38.614 --> 00:15:41.408
- No, we're on the top.
- Daylight and everything.

00:15:41.533 --> 00:15:44.161
- Oh.
- It must be wonderful.

00:15:44.244 --> 00:15:45.287
Meh.

00:15:45.370 --> 00:15:48.165
Listen, we actually came down here
to find our pet, Nibbler.

00:15:48.248 --> 00:15:49.875
He got flushed down the toilet.

00:15:49.958 --> 00:15:51.793
Well, if he got flushed down the toilet,

00:15:51.877 --> 00:15:53.629
he probably came through here.

00:15:54.171 --> 00:15:55.547
Everything always does.

00:15:55.964 --> 00:15:57.341
Follow me.

00:15:58.467 --> 00:16:01.511
All that is ours
was once flushed down your toilets.

00:16:01.887 --> 00:16:03.847
Over there is our aquarium.

00:16:04.348 --> 00:16:05.974
This is our library.

00:16:06.058 --> 00:16:08.602
Nothing but crumpled porno and Ayn Rand.

00:16:08.685 --> 00:16:10.520
And over here is our church.

00:16:12.689 --> 00:16:16.151
Wow. You guys worship
an unexploded nuclear bomb?

00:16:16.235 --> 00:16:17.945
Yeah, but nobody's that observant.

00:16:18.028 --> 00:16:20.197
It's mainly a Christmas and Easter thing.

00:16:21.281 --> 00:16:22.866
Nibbler?

00:16:22.950 --> 00:16:25.744
Come to Daddy, sweetie-ookums.

00:16:25.827 --> 00:16:28.247
So, is it true that alligators
flushed down the toilet

00:16:28.330 --> 00:16:29.456
survive down here?

00:16:29.539 --> 00:16:31.375
No. That's just an urban legend.

00:16:31.458 --> 00:16:32.751
Then what are those?

00:16:32.834 --> 00:16:33.835
Crocodiles.

00:16:33.919 --> 00:16:35.128
We keep them as pets.

00:16:35.212 --> 00:16:36.964
Then, when they grow too large

00:16:37.047 --> 00:16:39.299
we flush them down into the sub-sewer.

00:16:39.383 --> 00:16:42.844
Some say there's a freakish race
of sub-mutants down there.

00:16:42.928 --> 00:16:45.514
Please, that's just a sub-urban legend.

00:16:45.639 --> 00:16:48.600
Oh? Then I suppose
you also don't believe in...

00:16:48.725 --> 00:16:50.561
El Chupanibre.

00:16:52.604 --> 00:16:55.107
El Chupanibre? What's that?

00:16:59.027 --> 00:17:02.447
Gather 'round, children,
for the legend of El Chupanibre.

00:17:03.156 --> 00:17:06.076
He creeps and crawls
In the midnight hush

00:17:06.159 --> 00:17:08.787
Silent as a low-flow toilet flush

00:17:08.870 --> 00:17:10.998
Watch your step,
'Cause sooner or later

00:17:11.081 --> 00:17:13.834
He'll eat you whole
And half your alligator

00:17:13.917 --> 00:17:15.335
- Crocodile.
- Whatever.

00:17:15.919 --> 00:17:19.089
Wait, our pet Nibbler
loves fresh crocodile.

00:17:19.172 --> 00:17:20.632
It's his favorite treat.

00:17:20.716 --> 00:17:23.051
He must be El Chupanibre.

00:17:23.135 --> 00:17:24.428
Hey, yeah.

00:17:24.511 --> 00:17:27.431
You unleashed
the dreaded El Chupanibre upon us?

00:17:27.514 --> 00:17:29.808
Then you are our sworn enemies.

00:17:32.352 --> 00:17:33.562
You don't understand.

00:17:33.645 --> 00:17:35.314
He would never hurt people.

00:17:35.397 --> 00:17:36.773
Let us help you capture him.

00:17:36.857 --> 00:17:37.900
Impossible.

00:17:37.983 --> 00:17:39.151
If the legend is true,

00:17:39.234 --> 00:17:41.737
our only hope is to offer him
a snack-rifice.

00:17:41.862 --> 00:17:44.364
Yes, an unspoiled virgin.

00:17:44.448 --> 00:17:45.574
I volunteer.

00:17:45.657 --> 00:17:47.034
Nice try, Leela.

00:17:47.117 --> 00:17:49.578
But we've all seen
Zapp Brannigan's web page.

00:17:52.247 --> 00:17:54.875
Oh! I made myself feel bad.

00:17:54.958 --> 00:17:57.544
She'll have to do. Chain her to the post.

00:17:59.254 --> 00:18:01.089
And rip her shirt a little.

00:18:03.258 --> 00:18:07.721
Behold. When El Chupanibre
comes for the "virgin",

00:18:07.804 --> 00:18:09.806
he will be snared by this rope trap.

00:18:09.932 --> 00:18:12.851
Shh. El Chupanibre comes soon.

00:18:12.935 --> 00:18:14.019
It is nightfall.

00:18:14.102 --> 00:18:16.355
Nightfall? How can you tell down here?

00:18:18.565 --> 00:18:20.108
The tide is coming in.

00:18:20.192 --> 00:18:22.319
Quiet. The beast approaches.

00:18:38.126 --> 00:18:39.169
Nibbler!

00:18:39.253 --> 00:18:41.004
Come here, precious.

00:18:41.338 --> 00:18:44.091
Look, everyone, it's El Chupanibre.

00:18:44.174 --> 00:18:46.301
- That's not El Chupanibre.
- Say what?

00:18:46.385 --> 00:18:47.678
That's El Chupanibre.

00:18:54.184 --> 00:18:55.769
I'll take care of this.

00:19:05.070 --> 00:19:06.488
Bender, do something.

00:19:06.572 --> 00:19:07.864
I'm too scared.

00:19:07.948 --> 00:19:11.368
Leela, your scaredness
is being transmitted straight to Bender.

00:19:11.451 --> 00:19:14.204
If you care about Nibbler,
stop caring about him.

00:19:14.288 --> 00:19:15.330
I can't.

00:19:15.414 --> 00:19:16.915
I love every living creature.

00:19:16.999 --> 00:19:18.667
- Even me?
- As a friend.

00:19:18.750 --> 00:19:20.627
Damn.

00:19:20.794 --> 00:19:21.962
Listen to me, Leela.

00:19:22.045 --> 00:19:23.880
I'm an expert at not caring.

00:19:23.964 --> 00:19:27.926
The secret is to stop giving a rat's ass
about anyone else

00:19:28.010 --> 00:19:30.596
and start thinking of
the things that you want,

00:19:30.679 --> 00:19:32.222
that you deserve,

00:19:32.306 --> 00:19:34.349
that the world owes you.

00:19:35.684 --> 00:19:37.978
Well, I could use a new tank top.

00:19:38.061 --> 00:19:39.563
Bigger. Bigger!

00:19:39.646 --> 00:19:41.315
A fashionable tank top,

00:19:41.398 --> 00:19:44.776
and designer boots encrusted with jewels.

00:19:44.860 --> 00:19:45.861
Don't stop now.

00:19:45.944 --> 00:19:47.988
You'll need some pants
to go with that outfit.

00:19:48.071 --> 00:19:49.072
Yeah.

00:19:49.156 --> 00:19:50.407
And I could afford it all

00:19:50.490 --> 00:19:53.285
if I didn't have to feed
that stupid Nibbler.

00:19:53.368 --> 00:19:54.870
Bender is back.

00:19:54.953 --> 00:19:56.580
I'll save you, Nibbler.

00:20:03.337 --> 00:20:04.671
Oh.

00:20:06.298 --> 00:20:07.799
Bender's gonna be killed!

00:20:07.883 --> 00:20:09.301
You know what else I could use?

00:20:09.384 --> 00:20:11.678
A weekend at one of those fancy spas.

00:20:11.762 --> 00:20:12.804
And a Toblerone.

00:20:32.074 --> 00:20:33.533
Yay! You did it!

00:20:35.869 --> 00:20:38.080
Let's have a tissue tape parade.

00:20:38.163 --> 00:20:39.289
No, thanks.

00:20:46.046 --> 00:20:48.757
Gather 'round, children,
to hear the legend of Bender.

00:20:49.800 --> 00:20:52.094
He came from above with...

00:20:53.428 --> 00:20:54.721
It's going to be many a year

00:20:54.805 --> 00:20:57.307
before someone flushes
another guitar string.

00:21:00.394 --> 00:21:02.187
That was a disgusting story.

00:21:02.271 --> 00:21:04.147
And it's all thanks to Bender.

00:21:04.231 --> 00:21:05.440
I love you, Bender.

00:21:05.524 --> 00:21:06.942
I love you, too.

00:21:07.150 --> 00:21:10.654
Get that stupid chip out of me
before I kill myself.

00:21:14.032 --> 00:21:16.034
Bender, you won't believe this,

00:21:16.118 --> 00:21:18.328
but the empathy chip burned out.

00:21:18.412 --> 00:21:22.082
The emotion you felt for Nibbler
was actually your own.

00:21:22.499 --> 00:21:24.710
Huh. Looks like Bender learned
an important lesson

00:21:24.793 --> 00:21:27.754
about respecting
other people's feelings after all.

00:21:27.921 --> 00:21:29.339
Mm-hmm.

00:21:29.464 --> 00:21:30.924
No, I'm wrong.

00:21:31.008 --> 00:21:33.844
The empathy chip was running
at triple capacity.

00:21:33.927 --> 00:21:36.263
And I still barely felt anything.

00:21:37.055 --> 00:21:38.515
Good night, losers.

00:21:40.100 --> 00:21:43.020
You know, Bender may not
have learned anything from me,

00:21:43.103 --> 00:21:45.898
but I think I actually learned
something from him.

00:21:46.398 --> 00:21:48.066
So long, jerkwads!

00:21:48.609 --> 00:21:50.193
So long.